  "repair_or_experiment_note": "Completed the Step7 independent rigid-body mass DR round: 4096 envs, 2400.147 s, eight complete five-minute checkpoints with verified SHA receipts and nominal replays. Archived all saved final training/evaluation evidence, reward/command diagnostics, and large artifact indexes; retained original failed probe reports.\n\nPaired frozen-weight PhysX evaluation covered parent plus eight checkpoints, nominal and actual Step7+mass DR, eight tasks, ten initial states (1440 envs): no reset or numerical termination, max closure 0.764305 mm. Final actual-DR forward commands 2.0/2.2 produced 1.90307/2.15548 m/s, with 8/10 and 9/10 under the existing tracking protocol. The additional 2.7 command produced 2.61062 m/s without reset. Forward capability has recovered in tested conditions; remaining per-state tracking misses are preserved. Nominal MuJoCo speed bias is reported separately; no deployment graduation inferred.\n\nUpdated project and trial READMEs with completed status, exact final checkpoint identity, cumulative DR priorities (output scale -> body-part contact materials -> velocity push), the remaining target-range items, and the Flat-to-Rough continuation plan. Existing Rough generator has graded terrain but the direct environment does not yet connect performance-based terrain level updates; integrate low initial levels and progression when starting Rough, and retain current DR/timing/closure behavior. This phase starts no new training and changes no physical model or active controller.\n\nFinal checkpoint iteration 21754, SHA256 23c112b16e9629215c7265124925daaf0f9b6bbbb62be61689c714ba1fc7a772; 040m and final byte-identical. Parent iteration 21234, SHA256 74c25dd19708148808d1928fc4d6eb1278239fcdc6ab97598d866cf477dc561f. Weights and NPZ stay outside Git.\n",
